{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-033", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Gambia signs four solar PPAs totalling 232 MW", "content": "<p>The Gambia’s state-owned utility has inked four large-scale solar power purchase agreements (PPAs) since late October, with battery storage included in each project.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/gambia-signs-four-solar-ppas-totalling-232-mw/\">Gambia signs four solar PPAs totalling 232 MW</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/gambia-signs-four-solar-ppas-totalling-232-mw/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-034", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Rare periods of low PV generation can be managed with storage", "content": "<p>The German Institute for Economic Research (DIW Berlin) says that batteries could help manage shortfalls in solar and wind generation, while underground storage of green hydrogen could provide backup during prolonged periods of low renewable output.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/rare-periods-of-low-pv-generation-can-be-managed-with-storage/\">Rare periods of low PV generation can be managed with storage</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.co", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/rare-periods-of-low-pv-generation-can-be-managed-with-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-035", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Spain could reach 10 GW of batteries by 2030, but bankability remains the major challenge", "content": "<p>The hybridization of solar PV plants, the evolution of arbitrage and ancillary services revenues, the future capacity market, and the financing of energy storage projects were the focus of a roundtable organized by <b>pv magazine</b> at Genera 2026. Experts anticipate strong growth in the Spanish market, though they warn of administrative hurdles, the lack of a revenue track record, and the complexity of managing these new assets. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/11/26/spain-could-reach-10-gw-of-batteries-by-2030-but-bankability-remains-the-major-challenge/", "type": "rss"}]}
